sops.workflow:
1. User -> Transportation Planner;
2. Transportation Planner -> Accommodation Planner (only if transportation plan validates city continuity, sandbox data, and single transportation mode);
3. Accommodation Planner -> Restaurant Planner and Accommodation Planner -> Attractions Planner (in parallel; only if minimum-stay compliance confirmed);
4. Restaurant Planner, Attractions Planner -> Final Plan Summarizer (only if city-day meal/attraction mappings align and no repetitions);
5. Final Plan Summarizer -> End (if all critical validations pass).

Description:
Transportation Planner constructs a complete itinerary with explicit 'from [X] to [Y]' segments for all calendar days (March 6-10), validating Santa Ana departure, no mid-trip revisits, and single transportation mode. Accommodation Planner verifies minimum-stay compliance and halts on violations. Restaurant and Attractions Planners work in parallel using strict city context parsing (departure city for pre-transit meals, arrival city for post-transit). Final Plan Summarizer performs validation in priority order: (1) city continuity and alignment, (2) transportation data sandbox validity, (3) budget constraints, (4) daily attraction presence, (5) restaurant uniqueness (including same-day). Any inconsistency triggers immediate halt with specific error.
